        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.oboInOwllibrary.org/oboInOwl/po#Poaceae"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.oboInOwllibrary.org/oboInOwl/po#Rice"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.oboInOwllibrary.org/oboInOwl/po#TraitNet"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A fruit (PO:0009001) may contain additional plant structures (PO:0009011) that were part of a flower (PO:0009046) and mature along with the gynoecium, such as a receptacle (PO:0009064). A fruit may develop without fertilization in cases of parthenocarpy, apomixis, or other hormone-induced conditions and may not always contain seeds (PO:0009010). When annotating to fruit (PO:0009001) that are referred to as ‘aggregate’, ‘multiple’, or ‘compound’, please annotate directly to the appropriate plant structure, such as receptacle, hypanthium (PO:0009065) or infructescence (PO:0006342). Fruits only occur in angiosperms.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>fruit</rdfs:label>
